          "learn.read": "Guide read",
          "learn.unread": "Guide unread",
          "learn.libraryIntro": "Choose a feature to review purpose, steps, costs, and saving.",
          "learn.captain.0": "The Idle King approaches enemies to attack.\nTap ground to move or tap an enemy to approach and strike.",
          "learn.captain.1": "Use + in Idle King to level up.\nLevels increase damage, and training milestones shorten the attack interval.",
          "learn.captain.2": "Upgrades cost coins.\nCheck the total for ×1, ×10, ×100, or Max.\nLiu Bei unlocks at Idle King level 5.",
          "learn.squad.0": "Deployed warriors attack automatically.\nAll recruited warriors can fight alongside the captain.",
          "learn.squad.1": "Choose a warrior in Warband.\nOpen the profile → card → Warband to deploy or withdraw.\nDeployed warriors appear first with a check tag.",
          "learn.squad.2": "A first hire pays the shown single cost for level 1.\nLater upgrades use your selected quantity and total cost.\nCompare Combat, Growth, Gear, and Warband card tabs.",
          "learn.equipment.0": "Gear improves damage and coin multipliers.\nCompare Current → Selected before swapping.",
          "learn.equipment.1": "Choose gear in Equipment.\nUse Equip, Protect from sale, or Register in its details.\nTap a stat or i icon to read the effect.",
          "learn.equipment.2": "Equipping, swapping, and registration are free.\nCrafting uses gear shards; selling consumes the gear.\nCheck the actual diamond payout on Sell.",
          "learn.drones.0": "Divine Beasts support coins, Idle King damage, or warrior damage.\nDeploy up to three different divine beasts in fleet slots.",
          "learn.drones.1": "Divine Beasts → Manage Fleet → choose a slot and divine beast.\nRead its actual effect and level in Details.\nOpen a ready supply crate for a new divine beast.",
          "learn.drones.2": "Deployed divine beasts apply 100% of their support.\nUndeployed efficiency is level/100, capped at 100%.\nBeast Training is a matching game for divine beast growth.",
          "learn.intel.0": "Owned intel applies lasting bonuses automatically.\nClassified Report 1, level 1: damage and coins ×1.22.",
          "learn.intel.1": "Current sector 60 → Campaign Renewal in Idle King → Intel Points.\nAcquire, inspect, and upgrade records in Intel.\nBalance: {points} · New record: {cost}.",
          "learn.intel.2": "Acquisition and upgrades spend Intel Points.\nA new record is random among unowned records.\nSalvage: 20 diamonds, 80% of upgrade investment back.",
          "learn.supply.0": "Supply contains free rewards and optional purchases.\nIcons and colors distinguish currencies and categories.",
          "learn.supply.1": "Choose General, Growth, or Limited offers.\nInspect contents, price, and claim conditions.\nClaim now appears only for a reward you can receive.",
          "learn.supply.2": "Distinguish free, coin, diamond, and paid offers.\nGray buttons mean a cost or service condition is unmet.\nTap the button to read the specific reason.",
          "learn.redeploy.0": "Campaign Renewal resets your current combat growth.\nEarn Intel Points for lasting intel records.",
          "learn.redeploy.1": "Idle King → Campaign Renewal → review what resets.\nEstimated Intel Points: {reward}.\nNothing resets until you confirm the real action.",
          "learn.redeploy.2": "Campaign Renewal requires current sector 60 or higher.\nSector, Idle King/warrior levels, and coins reset.\nReading or closing confirmation spends nothing.",
          "learn.tactics.0": "Tactics use energy and cooldowns in combat.\nTheir damage, critical, coin, and duration effects differ.",
          "learn.tactics.1": "Idle King → Tactic Slots → pick one of six → replace.\nHide the menu to use the battlefield tactic buttons.\nThe same tactic keeps its icon in every view.",
          "learn.tactics.2": "Casting uses energy; upgrades use coins.\nCheck the Idle King unlock level and remaining cooldown.\nCompare actual effect, duration, and stacks in Details.",
          "learn.registry.0": "The equipment registry records your collected gear.\nIt is separate from the warrior character codex.",
          "learn.registry.1": "Open gear Details → Register.\nReview registration and total bonuses in the registry.\nA green button marks Registered.",
          "learn.registry.2": "Registration is free and does not consume gear.\nAcquire missing gear first.\nCompleted entries cannot be registered twice.",
          "learn.rewards.0": "Check daily, achievement, sector, supply, and offline rewards.\nClaim now appears only for an actual available reward.",
          "learn.rewards.1": "Review goals and progress in Ops.\nRead the reward icons and amounts in the claim window.\nChoose Camp claim or Ad ×2.",
          "learn.rewards.2": "Camp claim grants the shown reward without an ad.\nAd ×2 adds the same reward after verification.\nWeb and test builds allow doubling without ads.",
          "learn.skills.0": "Talents give lasting growth through six branches and 18 nodes.\nChoose nodes for their actual damage or coin effects.",
          "learn.skills.1": "Select a node → edit with +/− → compare effects.\nApply saves your edited training.\nUndo discards only unapplied edits.",
          "learn.skills.2": "The next level costs edited level +1 points.\nHigher tiers require predecessor level 3.\nCompare saved/draft factors and remaining points.",
          "learn.skills.3": "Applied talents survive discharge.\nUnapplied edits are separate from actual stats.\nReview the refund scope before returning or resetting.",
          "learn.part.3": "Save & cautions",
          "learn.exploration.0": "Supply Search has 16 hidden crates to uncover.\nFind and claim their diamond rewards.",
          "learn.exploration.1": "Ops → Special Ops → Supply Search.\nChoose a closed crate and check its cost.\nDistinguish open tiles from closed ones.",
          "learn.exploration.2": "Each crate costs 20 event tokens.\nCamp diamond rewards are 5, 10, or 15.\nReading the guide or map spends no tokens.",
          "learn.exploration.3": "Opened crates and claim status are saved.\nThe same tile cannot pay twice.\nCheck overall completion and season time remaining.",
          "learn.cards.0": "The card deck holds ability cards for raids.\nIt is separate from your warrior combat deck.",
          "learn.cards.1": "Ops → Cards → open Details.\nRead effects and choose three cards for the deck.\nReview your deck before entering a raid.",
          "learn.cards.2": "Cards unlock at best sector 100.\nCheck the shown shards and costs for fusion or growth.\nReading and comparing cards is free.",
          "learn.raids.0": "Raids are timed battles against enemy parts.\nTheir card effects are separate from normal sector combat.",
          "learn.raids.1": "Ops → Solo Raid → review three cards.\nSelect a portal → attack parts → claim the result.\nWatch remaining time and part health.",
          "learn.raids.2": "Raids unlock at best sector 100.\nCheck portal and daily-goal claim status.\nRegiment raids follow account, entry, and server-card rules.",
          "learn.events.0": "Special Ops are seasonal rewards using event tokens.\nCumulative goals and supply search follow different rules.",
          "learn.events.1": "Ops → Special Ops → review cumulative goals.\nClaim rewards for completed goals.\nOpen Supply Search separately to uncover crates.",
          "learn.events.2": "Milestone claims are free.\nOpening search crates spends event tokens.\nCompare your balance with the required amount first.",
          "learn.growth.0": "Advanced Growth includes gems, research, support, and monuments.\nEach system has its own currency and unlock condition.",
          "learn.growth.1": "Ops → Advanced Growth or More Growth.\nCompare the stat, current/next effect, and cost.\nUse that system’s growth action after reviewing.",
          "learn.growth.2": "Gems and research unlock at best sector 1,000.\nSupport unlocks at sector 100,000 or account age 30 days.\nMonuments require best sector 180,000.",
          "intel.effect.0": "All damage & coin gain",
          "intel.effect.1": "Idle King tap damage",
